<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Ryten and Kvalvika from Innersand — Innersand–Ryten inner summit–Kvalvika return [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>From the signed paid Innersand parking area, follow the prepared entry by Einangen to the Forsvatnet junction. Visit Ryten first by the mapped inner summit branch, staying well back from all cliff edges and photo positions. Return to the junction, descend to the Kvalvika beach walking terminus, then retrace the course to Innersand.

Plan for demanding rough and steep mountain terrain, wet rock, bog, steps and consequential cliff exposure. Choose dry, snow-free conditions with adequate daylight; rain, ice, snow and strong coastal wind can change feasibility. Mapped bridges and a chain barrier do not guarantee current passage. Follow current onsite closures, signs and marked diversions. The June 22–September 30, 2026 construction notice is historical; the linked park current-conditions page was unavailable during verification, so current conditions remain unverified.

Use designated paid parking and check the current fee. Leash dogs April 1–November 15 and follow current rules; avoid disturbing sheep, birds and nesting sites. Protect vegetation and cultural remains, take litter out and do not fly drones in the national park.

Allow approximately 9.1 km, 610 m ascent and descent and five hours. The distance is rounded from the mapped line; ascent, descent and time remain approximate legacy planning figures without surveyed elevations. This two-dimensional line is for trip planning, not navigation, an easy or nontechnical guarantee, or an assurance of safety.

